# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the object store and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true writes CRLF, and
# Biome, which defaults to LF, then reports a format error on every file it
# reads. That produced 232 diagnostics with zero rule violations, which makes
# `pnpm lint` unreadable locally while staying green in CI. A gate nobody can
# read is a gate nobody runs.
#
# `text=auto` still detects binary files and leaves them alone. The explicit
# `-text` lines below are belt and braces for the formats where a corrupted
# byte is silent rather than obvious.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png -text
*.pdf -text
*.pptx -text
*.ico -text
*.woff -text
*.woff2 -text
